IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hdsc-dates`
IMPORT `hdsc-complaints`

-- Health and Disability Services (Complaints) Act 1995 (WA) -- worked cases for the questions of the person making a
-- complaint.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`1 Jan 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 1 2024
`28 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 28 2 2024
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 29 2 2024
`1 Mar 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 3 2024
`7 Nov 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 7 11 2024
`31 Dec 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 31 12 2024
`29 Feb 2000` MEANS `the calendar day` 29 2 2000
`28 Feb 2002` MEANS `the calendar day` 28 2 2002
`1 Jan 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 1 2026
`2 Jan 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 2 1 2026
`28 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 28 2 2026
`1 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 3 2026
`1 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 10 2026
`15 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 15 10 2026
`16 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 16 10 2026
`29 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 29 10 2026
`31 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 31 10 2026
`6 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 6 11 2026
`7 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 7 11 2026
`8 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 8 11 2026
`15 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 15 11 2026
`16 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 16 11 2026
`20 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 20 11 2026
`26 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 26 11 2026
`30 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 30 11 2026
`1 Dec 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 12 2026
`10 Dec 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 10 12 2026
`31 Dec 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 31 12 2026

-- s 3 health service
`HS YES` MEANS `yes: it is a health service under s 3, so a complaint about it can be made under this Act`
`HS EXCLUDED` MEANS `no: it was provided without payment in a rescue or emergency, so it is an excluded service and not a health service (s 3, the text's no); the Director may refer a complaint about it elsewhere with your written consent (s 28)`
`HS NOT LISTED` MEANS `no: it is not a service of any kind listed in the definition of health service (s 3, a "means" definition: the text's no)`

-- s 25(1) matters
`(a)` MEANS `s 25(1)(a): a provider acted unreasonably by not providing a health service for the user`
`(b)` MEANS `s 25(1)(b): a provider acted unreasonably in the manner of providing a health service for the user`
`(c)` MEANS `s 25(1)(c): a provider acted unreasonably in providing a health service for the user`
`(g)` MEANS `s 25(1)(g): a provider charged the user an excessive fee or otherwise acted unreasonably about a fee`
`(h)` MEANS `s 25(1)(h): a provider that is an applicable organisation failed to comply with the Carers Charter`
`(i)` MEANS `s 25(1)(i): a health care worker failed to comply with a code of conduct that applies to them`
`(j)` MEANS `s 25(1)(j): a health care worker failed to comply with an interim prohibition order`
`(k)` MEANS `s 25(1)(k): a health care worker failed to comply with a prohibition order`
`no matter` MEANS `none of the matters in s 25(1)`

-- who I am
`user` MEANS `the user: I used or received the health service, or was the subject of the research`
`chosen` MEANS `a person the user chose to complain on the user's behalf`
`unchosen` MEANS `a person the user did not choose, complaining for a user who has died or cannot complain or choose`
`carer` MEANS `a carer of the user`
`provider` MEANS `a provider complaining for the user about a health service another provider gave the user`
`arranger` MEANS `a person who only arranged the health service for the user`
`anyone` MEANS `any other person`

`AS USER` MEANS `yes: as the user you may complain about this matter (s 19(1)(a))`
`ANY PERSON` MEANS `yes: any person may complain about this matter (s 19(3))`
`AS REP` MEANS `yes: as the user's representative recognised by the Director (s 19(1)(b), s 20)`
`AS CARER` MEANS `yes: as a carer you may complain that the Carers Charter was not complied with (s 19(2))`
`AS PROVIDER` MEANS `yes: as a provider for whom s 22 applies (s 19(1)(c), s 22)`
`REP BARRED` MEANS `no: the Director may not recognise you as a representative, because you are paid for it or have a financial interest in the outcome and are not a relative (s 20(3), the text's no)`
`UNCHOSEN NO` MEANS `no: a person the user did not choose can be recognised only if the user has died or cannot complain or choose, and you have a sufficient interest (s 20(2), the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`PROVIDER NO` MEANS `no: a provider may complain for the user only if the user has died or it would be difficult or impossible for the user to complain (s 22, the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`ARRANGER NO` MEANS `no: a person who only arranged the service is not a user (s 3 user, the text's no); you may complain as the user's representative if the Director recognises you`
`NO MATTER NO` MEANS `no: a complaint must allege one of the matters in s 25(1) (s 25(1), s 26(1)(c), the text's no)`
`REP NOT YET` MEANS `not yet: you may complain as the user's representative once the Director recognises you (s 19(1)(b), s 20(1); the Act lists no other route: NOTHING-kind)`
`NOT LISTED` MEANS `s 19 does not list you for this matter; you may complain as the user's representative if the Director recognises you (NOTHING-kind)`

-- s 24
`IN TIME` MEANS `in time: made no more than 24 months after the incident (s 24)`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `still in time: not yet made, and 24 months since the incident have not passed (s 24)`
`LATE GOOD REASON` MEANS `late, but the Director finds you have shown good reason for the delay, so s 24 does not require rejection`
`MUST REJECT LATE` MEANS `the Director must reject it: more than 24 months after the incident, without good reason for the delay (s 24, the text's no)`

-- s 27
`INFO YES` MEANS `yes: given within the time the Director fixed (s 27(5))`
`INFO NOT YET` MEANS `not yet, and there is still time: give it by the last day the Director fixed (s 27(5))`
`INFO LATE` MEANS `no: not given within the time the Director fixed, so the Director may reject your complaint (s 27(6))`

-- ss 24-30
`R S28` MEANS `it is about an excluded service: the Director may refer it to an appropriate person or body with your written consent (s 28)`
`R S24` MEANS `the Director must reject it: more than 24 months after the incident, without good reason for the delay (s 24)`
`R S26 1ab` MEANS `the Director must reject it: in the Director's opinion it is vexatious, trivial or without substance, or does not warrant further action (s 26(1)(a), (b))`
`R S26 1c` MEANS `the Director must reject it: in the Director's opinion it does not comply with this Act (s 26(1)(c))`
`R S26 2` MEANS `the Director must reject it to the extent it raises an issue already decided by a court, the State Administrative Tribunal, an industrial tribunal or a registration board (s 26(2))`
`R S27` MEANS `the Director may reject it: you did not confirm it in writing, give your name and identity details, or give the further information required (s 27(6))`
`R S30` MEANS `the Director may reject it: the Director is not satisfied that reasonable steps were taken to resolve the matter with the provider (s 30)`
`R NONE` MEANS `none of ss 24, 26, 27, 28 and 30 stands in the way: the Director must decide whether to accept it within 28 days of receiving it (s 34(1))`

-- s 34
`P INVESTIGATE 5A` MEANS `the Director must investigate it (s 34(5A))`
`P ANY OF THREE` MEANS `the Director must attempt a negotiated settlement, refer it for conciliation, or investigate it (s 34(5))`
`P NEG OR CONC` MEANS `the Director must attempt a negotiated settlement or refer it for conciliation (s 34(4)(a), (b))`
`P NEG` MEANS `the Director must attempt a negotiated settlement (s 34(4)(a))`
`P CONC` MEANS `the Director must refer it for conciliation (s 34(4)(b))`
`P INVESTIGATE 4c` MEANS `the Director must investigate it, as it is suitable for neither settlement nor conciliation and an investigation is warranted (s 34(4)(c))`
`P NO FURTHER` MEANS `no further action: the Director must tell you so in writing (s 34(6)(b))`
`P ASSUMES` MEANS `this question assumes a complaint about one of the matters in s 25(1)`

-- steps
`S32A` MEANS `s 32A: the Director tells me a National Board is dealing with my complaint (28 days from the Board beginning to deal with it)`
`S33` MEANS `s 33(a): the Director tells me my complaint has been referred to another body (28 days from the referral)`
`S34` MEANS `s 34(1): the Director decides whether to accept my complaint (28 days from receiving it, extendable by up to 28 days)`
`S35` MEANS `s 35(1): the Director gives the provider written notice of accepting my complaint (14 days from deciding to accept it)`
`S36A` MEANS `s 36A(3): the provider gives its written response (28 days from receiving the notice, or longer if the Director extends it)`
`S36B` MEANS `s 36B(3): negotiation ends, and the Director must refer the complaint for conciliation or investigate it (56 days from complying with s 35, or longer if extended)`
`S37` MEANS `s 37(1): the conciliator gives me written notice of the referral for conciliation (14 days from the referral)`
`S40a` MEANS `s 40(4)(a): I get a copy of the conciliator's final report (the same day it is made to the Director)`
`S40b` MEANS `s 40(4)(b): the provider's registration board gets a copy of the conciliator's final report (30 days from the report)`
`S44` MEANS `s 44(2): the Director gives the provider written notice of an investigation (14 days from commencing it)`
`S50` MEANS `s 50(2): the Director gives me written notice of the decision after an investigation (14 days from the decision)`
`S51` MEANS `s 51(1): the provider reports what it has done to remedy the matter (45 days from receiving the s 50(2) notice, extendable by up to 15 days)`
`S52` MEANS `s 52(1): the Director gives me written notice of stopping dealing with an issue (14 days from stopping)`

-- s 51
`REPORTED` MEANS `yes: the provider reported within the time allowed (s 51(1))`
`REPORT NOT YET` MEANS `not yet, and the provider still has time to report (s 51(1))`
`LATE AND MINISTER` MEANS `no: the provider did not report in time, an offence with a penalty of up to $2 500 (s 51(1)); the Director must give the Minister the notice and a report on the failure (s 52A(1))`
`LATE ONLY` MEANS `no: the provider did not report in time, an offence with a penalty of up to $2 500 (s 51(1))`

-- s 29, 39, 41, 43
`W STOP` MEANS `the Director must stop dealing with it and, if the provider was given notice, tell the provider (s 29(1))`
`W GOES ON` MEANS `the Director has decided to go on dealing with it, as it alleges a breach of a code of conduct or a prohibition order; the Director need not give you further information about it (s 29(2), (3))`
`REP IN CONC` MEANS `yes: the Director has determined that conciliation will not work effectively without representation (s 39(1))`
`NO REP IN CONC` MEANS `no: neither you nor the provider may be represented in conciliation unless the Director so determines (s 39(1), the text's no); others may still attend if the conciliator thinks they will help (s 39(2))`
`TELL DIRECTOR` MEANS `you must tell the Director without delay (s 41(2)); once the Director or conciliator knows, they must stop dealing with the complaint (s 41(3))`
`DIRECTOR STOPS` MEANS `the Director or conciliator, now aware, must stop dealing with the complaint (s 41(3))`
`C MAY` MEANS `the Director may investigate it, refer it again for conciliation, or deal with it in another way the Act allows (s 43(2))`
`C ASKED` MEANS `the Director must not take it further unless you ask; you have asked, so the Director may investigate, refer it again for conciliation, or deal with it in another way (s 43(1))`
`C MUST NOT` MEANS `the Director must not investigate it, refer it again for conciliation or deal with it in any other way, unless you ask (s 43(1), the text's no)`
`C AGREED` MEANS `the conciliator's final report records the agreement (s 40(2)(a)); the Act sets no further step for the Director (NOTHING-kind)`

-- s 52
`L 1A` MEANS `s 52 does not apply to a complaint about a code of conduct or a prohibition order (s 52(1A), the text's no)`
`L REOPEN` MEANS `the Director may reopen the complaint with your consent, the proceedings having been withdrawn or abandoned (s 52(3))`
`L STOP CONC` MEANS `the Director must stop dealing with the issue and tell you in writing within 14 days, but may refer the complaint for conciliation, with both your and the provider's consent, until the hearing begins (s 52(1), (4))`
`L STOP` MEANS `the Director must stop dealing with the issue and tell you in writing within 14 days (s 52(1))`
`L INVESTIGATE` MEANS `the Director may still investigate the matter so as to take part in the further proceedings (s 52(2))`
`L NOT STOPPED` MEANS `s 52 does not stop the Director: none of its conditions is met (the text's no)`

-- s 71
`participant` MEANS `a participant in conciliation or an investigation, myself or as someone's agent`
`notice holder` MEANS `a person who received a notice from the Director or the conciliator about a complaint (ss 33, 35, 37, 50)`
`outsider` MEANS `none of these parts`

§ `s 3 -- is it a health service`

#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it a health service` `diagnosis or treatment of a physical or mental disorder or injury, or a suspected one (s 3 health service (a))` FALSE EQUALS `HS YES`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it a health service` `a service prescribed by regulations (s 3 health service (h))` FALSE EQUALS `HS YES`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it a health service` `medical or epidemiological research (s 3 health service (d))` FALSE EQUALS `HS YES`
-- An ambulance given free at a road accident: an excluded service.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it a health service` `an ambulance service (s 3 health service (e))` TRUE EQUALS `HS EXCLUDED`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it a health service` `none of the kinds listed` FALSE EQUALS `HS NOT LISTED`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- is it a health service` `none of the kinds listed` TRUE EQUALS `HS NOT LISTED`

§ `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint`

-- Arguments: matter, who I am, unpaid, relative, financial interest, user died or unable, sufficient interest, recognised,
-- user died or it is hard to complain.
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `no matter` `user` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO MATTER NO`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(i)` `anyone` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ANY PERSON`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(j)` `arranger` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ANY PERSON`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(k)` `user` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ANY PERSON`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(b)` `user` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AS USER`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(h)` `user` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AS USER`
-- A representative the user chose.
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(b)` `chosen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AS REP`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(b)` `chosen` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REP NOT YET`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(b)` `chosen` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REP BARRED`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(b)` `chosen` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REP BARRED`
-- A relative with a financial interest (an heir of a user who died) is not barred by s 20(3)(b).
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(b)` `chosen` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AS REP`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(b)` `chosen` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REP BARRED`
-- A representative the user did not choose (s 20(2)).
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(c)` `unchosen` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AS REP`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(c)` `unchosen` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `UNCHOSEN NO`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(c)` `unchosen` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `UNCHOSEN NO`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(c)` `unchosen` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REP BARRED`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(c)` `unchosen` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REP NOT YET`
-- A carer.
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(h)` `carer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AS CARER`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(a)` `carer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT LISTED`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(i)` `carer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ANY PERSON`
-- A provider complaining about another provider (s 22).
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(c)` `provider` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `AS PROVIDER`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(c)` `provider` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `PROVIDER NO`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(h)` `provider` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `AS PROVIDER`
-- A parent who only booked an adult child's appointment is not a user.
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(a)` `arranger` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ARRANGER NO`
#ASSERT `ss 19-22 -- may I make this complaint` `(g)` `anyone` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT LISTED`

§ `s 24 -- the last day and whether the complaint is in time`

#ASSERT `s 24 -- the last day to complain without showing good reason` `7 Nov 2024` EQUALS `7 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- the last day to complain without showing good reason` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `31 Dec 2026`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- the last day to complain without showing good reason` `1 Jan 2024` EQUALS `1 Jan 2026`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- the last day to complain without showing good reason` `28 Feb 2024` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- the last day to complain without showing good reason` `1 Mar 2024` EQUALS `1 Mar 2026`
-- 29 February with no 29 February two years on: 28 February (fork F2).
#ASSERT `s 24 -- the last day to complain without showing good reason` `29 Feb 2024` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- the last day to complain without showing good reason` `29 Feb 2000` EQUALS `28 Feb 2002`

-- Arguments: incident, made, made on, today, good reason.
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` TRUE `7 Nov 2026` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` TRUE `6 Nov 2026` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` TRUE `8 Nov 2026` `8 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `MUST REJECT LATE`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` TRUE `8 Nov 2026` `8 Nov 2026` TRUE EQUALS `LATE GOOD REASON`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` TRUE `7 Nov 2024` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- A complaint date before the incident is counted as day 0.
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` TRUE `1 Jan 2024` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `29 Feb 2024` TRUE `28 Feb 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `29 Feb 2024` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE EQUALS `MUST REJECT LATE`
-- Not yet made.
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2024` `7 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2024` `8 Nov 2026` FALSE EQUALS `MUST REJECT LATE`
#ASSERT `s 24 -- is my complaint in time` `7 Nov 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2024` `8 Nov 2026` TRUE EQUALS `LATE GOOD REASON`

-- The regulative rule alone (730 days from 7 Nov 2024 to 7 Nov 2026).
#ASSERT `the number of days from` `7 Nov 2024` `until` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS 730
#ASSERT `s 24 -- complaining on this day is in time` 730 0
#ASSERT `s 24 -- complaining on this day is in time` 730 730
#ASSERT NOT (`s 24 -- complaining on this day is in time` 730 731)

§ `s 27 -- further information`

-- Arguments: asked on, days fixed, given, given on, today. 14 days from 1 Oct 2026: last day 15 Oct 2026.
#ASSERT `s 27 -- have I given the further information in time` `1 Oct 2026` 14 TRUE `15 Oct 2026` `16 Oct 2026` EQUALS `INFO YES`
#ASSERT `s 27 -- have I given the further information in time` `1 Oct 2026` 14 TRUE `1 Oct 2026` `16 Oct 2026` EQUALS `INFO YES`
#ASSERT `s 27 -- have I given the further information in time` `1 Oct 2026` 14 TRUE `16 Oct 2026` `16 Oct 2026` EQUALS `INFO LATE`
#ASSERT `s 27 -- have I given the further information in time` `1 Oct 2026` 14 FALSE `1 Oct 2026` `15 Oct 2026` EQUALS `INFO NOT YET`
#ASSERT `s 27 -- have I given the further information in time` `1 Oct 2026` 14 FALSE `1 Oct 2026` `16 Oct 2026` EQUALS `INFO LATE`

§ `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected`

-- Arguments: excluded service, incident, made on, good reason, vexatious or no action warranted, does not comply, already
-- decided, about undecided matters, did what s 27 required, reasonable steps.
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R NONE`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` TRUE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R S28`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` TRUE `1 Jan 2024` `2 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R S28`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2024` `2 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R S24`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2024` `1 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R NONE`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2024` `2 Jan 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R NONE`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `R S26 1ab`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R S26 1c`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R S26 2`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R NONE`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `R S27`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `R S30`
#ASSERT `ss 24-30 -- will my complaint be rejected` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `R S27`

§ `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint`

-- Arguments: matter, suitable for settlement, suitable for conciliation, investigation warranted.
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `(j)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `P INVESTIGATE 5A`
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `(k)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `P INVESTIGATE 5A`
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `(i)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `P ANY OF THREE`
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `(a)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `P NEG OR CONC`
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `(c)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `P NEG`
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `(c)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `P CONC`
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `(c)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `P INVESTIGATE 4c`
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `(c)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `P NO FURTHER`
#ASSERT `s 34 -- what happens to my accepted complaint` `no matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `P ASSUMES`

§ `ss 32A-52 -- deadlines, and s 58`

-- Arguments: step, the period starts, extension days, extended for a delay.
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S34` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST `29 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S34` `1 Oct 2026` 28 FALSE EQUALS JUST `26 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S34` `1 Oct 2026` 40 FALSE EQUALS JUST `26 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S34` `1 Oct 2026` 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S35` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST `15 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S35` `1 Oct 2026` 5 TRUE EQUALS JUST `15 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S36A` `1 Oct 2026` 10 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`the calendar day` 8 11 2026)
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S36A` `1 Oct 2026` (0 MINUS 5) FALSE EQUALS JUST `29 Oct 2026`
#ASSERT `ss 32A-52 -- the last day for this step` `S36B` `1 Oct 2026` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST `26 Nov 2026`
